  "source": {
    "generator": null,
    "notes": "American put with a TIGHT primal-dual bracket. The primal (american_put) is the out-of-sample LSM lower bound. The tight dual (dual_tight) is the Andersen-Broadie-style upper bound built as the Doob martingale of the discounted-intrinsic process Y_t = disc^t*payoff_t, M_t = sum_{k<=t}(Y_k - E_{k-1}[Y_k]); the one-step conditional expectation E_{k-1}[Y_k] is estimated by NESTED SIMULATION (the nested_stat each_step operation, done natively): inner next-step states are resampled from the panel's own one-step log-returns (so no volatility parameter is needed) and the payoff is re-evaluated there. It is a genuine martingale, so the bound is valid, and it tracks the option far better than the single hedge -> the bracket tightens from ~[6.04, 9.70] to ~[6.04, 6.50]. dual_loose is the original single-hedge dual, kept for contrast. See AMERICAN_OPTION_SCOPE.md / AMERICAN_TIGHT_DUAL_EXAMPLE.md."
  },
